      "id": "C1",
      "question": "Q1",
      "subject": "S",
      "level": "descriptive",
      "text": "The well-formedness check in fvtrace check reports no violation exactly when the decoded trace is well-formed, and every violation it reports names a rule that the decoded trace breaks.",
      "needs": [
        "P1",
        "P2"
      ],
      "entailment": "E1"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "question": "Q2",
      "subject": "S",
      "level": "descriptive",
      "text": "With no what-if and without --cached, a claim reads Fully supported only when every fact it needs is verified and its evidence is unchanged since it was pinned.",
      "needs": [
        "P3",
        "T2",
        "I2"
      ],
      "entailment": "E2"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "question": "Q2",
      "subject": "S",
      "level": "descriptive",
      "text": "In a well-formed trace under a valid what-if, a claim whose reasoning fact is only human-ruled or empirical reads neither Fully supported nor Conditional.",
      "needs": [
        "P4"
      ],
      "entailment": "E3"
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "question": "Q2",
      "subject": "S",
      "level": "descriptive",
      "text": "Claim not possible holds exactly when a need is violated, the claim needs both sides of a verified or assumed exclusion, or both sides of such an exclusion hold on the claim's subject.",
      "needs": [
